%% ccl_uninames.pl -- THE UNICODE NAME TABLE for `\N{NAME}' (C++23 [lex.charset], C23 6.4.3; 0.103): one fact per
%% assigned character, `ccl_uname(Name, CodePoint)', the Name property of Unicode 14.0.0 as python3's unicodedata gives
%% it -- GENERATED by scratchpad tooling from that module, never edited by hand. The families whose names are their
%% code point's hex digits (CJK UNIFIED IDEOGRAPH-4E00, CJK COMPATIBILITY IDEOGRAPH-, TANGUT IDEOGRAPH-, KHITAN SMALL
%% SCRIPT CHARACTER-, NUSHU CHARACTER-) are computed by both lexers and are not here; the Hangul syllables are. The DCG
%% loads this file on the first `\N{' it meets (ccl_uname_lookup in ccl_syntax); module/build.sh spells the same facts
%% into module/ccl_uninames.h for the native lexer, so the table is written once. Name aliases (NameAliases.txt) are
%% not here: named in CLAUDE.md as not done.
